      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a deeply debated historical question with strong arguments on both sides. Supporters argue that the extreme violence was a necessary, if terrible, defense against internal and external threats to the Republic.\n\nHowever, critics view the systematic use of the guillotine as a fundamental moral breakdown, where the ideological purity of the Revolution justified immense state-sponsored violence against its own people. In the end, it likely involved a complex, tragic mix of political realpolitik and profound moral conviction.",
